---
// biome-ignore lint/correctness/noUnusedImports: Astro uses this layout component below.
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="FAQ | plansplease"
  description="Answers about the plansplease CLI, cloud workspace, privacy, and alpha plans."
  activePath="faq"
>
  <section class="faq-hero" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
    <div class="faq-hero-content">
      <span class="faq-badge">Help Center</span>
      <h1 id="faq-title">Questions we expect to hear.</h1>
      <p class="faq-lead">
        Clear, direct answers about how plansplease handles local loopback serving, private cloud
        vaults, and agent integrations.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="faq-content">
    <div class="faq-list">
      <details class="faq-item" open>
        <summary>
          <span>What is plansplease?</span>
          <span class="faq-toggle-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>
            plansplease gives agent-generated web artifacts a permanent, interactive home. Coding
            agents (Claude, Cursor, ChatGPT, Gemini) often output complete single-page tools,
            simulators, or dashboards.
          </p>
          <p>
            The plansplease CLI creates an instant, zero-latency local preview on your machine,
            while our cloud workspace securely archives your pages so they never get lost in a
            closed chat thread.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>
          <span>What file types and assets can I preview?</span>
          <span class="faq-toggle-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>
            The local CLI serves both standalone HTML files and multi-file directory bundles with an
            <code>index.html</code> entry point. You can include linked stylesheets, images, client-side
            JavaScript, Canvas scripts, and CDN-hosted libraries (like Tailwind, Chart.js, or React).
          </p>
          <p>
            The cloud workspace currently accepts standalone HTML files with full support for inline
            scripts and CDN dependencies.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>
          <span>Are my cloud pages public or private?</span>
          <span class="faq-toggle-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>
            Your pages are strictly private. Every cloud upload is tied exclusively to your
            authenticated GitHub account. Nobody else can view or access your uploaded artifacts
            unless you explicitly choose to share your screen.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>
          <span>Does the local CLI require internet access?</span>
          <span class="faq-toggle-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>
            No. The CLI runs entirely on your local machine using an isolated loopback daemon.
            It does not send your code, files, or previews to the cloud unless you explicitly use
            the cloud workspace.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>
          <span>Can I integrate plansplease directly with AI agents?</span>
          <span class="faq-toggle-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>
            Yes. The CLI supports headless automation, and plansplease provides Model Context
            Protocol (MCP) server hooks so agents like Claude Desktop and Cursor can publish and
            inspect artifacts programmatically during their execution loop.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary>
          <span>Can I self-host plansplease?</span>
          <span class="faq-toggle-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
        </summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">
          <p>
            The source code is 100% open source under the MIT license on
            <a href="https://github.com/abijith-suresh/planview">GitHub</a>. While our cloud managed
            service is currently in alpha, self-hosting configurations and container definitions
            are on our active roadmap.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  .faq-hero {
    padding: clamp(4rem, 7vh, 6rem) 0 3rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--night-border);
  }

  .faq-hero-content {
    max-width: 48rem;
  }

  .faq-badge {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 0.25rem 0.75rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
    border-radius: 9999px;
    background: var(--iris-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--iris-border);
    color: var(--iris);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .faq-hero h1 {
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
    color: var(--text-white);
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 4.4vw, 3.6rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    line-height: 1.1;
  }

  .faq-lead {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--night-muted);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .faq-content {
    padding: 4.5rem 0;
    max-width: 54rem;
  }

  .faq-list {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .faq-item {
    border: 1px solid var(--night-border);
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: var(--night-card);
    overflow: hidden;
    transition: border-color 160ms ease;
  }

  .faq-item:hover {
    border-color: var(--iris-border);
  }

  .faq-item summary {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    padding: 1.5rem 1.75rem;
    color: var(--text-white);
    cursor: pointer;
    font-family: var(--display);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .faq-item summary::-webkit-details-marker {
    display: none;
  }

  .faq-toggle-icon {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 28px;
    height: 28px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    background: var(--night-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--night-border);
    color: var(--night-muted);
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    transition: transform 180ms ease, color 180ms ease;
  }

  .faq-item[open] .faq-toggle-icon {
    transform: rotate(45deg);
    color: var(--mint);
  }

  .faq-answer {
    padding: 0 1.75rem 1.75rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--night-border);
    padding-top: 1.25rem;
  }

  .faq-answer p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    color: var(--night-muted);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .faq-answer p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .faq-answer code {
    color: var(--mint);
    background: var(--night);
    padding: 0.15rem 0.35rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.88em;
  }

  .faq-answer a {
    color: var(--mint);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
</style>
